\f1\fs22 Chanta put the finishing touches on a peanut butter, banana, and bacon sandwich. He was at the kitchen window, about to take the first bite, when a sound as terrifying as a screaming jet engine crashing through a gigantic drum kit assaulted him from behind. Still holding the sandwich inches from his mouth, he turned in mute shock as the mansion collapsed like a little pig\'92s house made of sticks and golden toilet bowls.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 He was regarding his sandwich, considering whether he could take it with him, when a ghostly plume of dust whooshed from the wreckage and layered his beloved meal with grit.\
He ran outside, weaving around what was still standing of the mansion, fearing the parlour would be a pile of rubble. He was sure Sarah was in there, and now was not the time to lose her. He stopped when he saw the degree of damage: there wasn\'92t any. It was a miracle. He nearly wept. From just off the parlour verandah, the mansion looked as pristine as the day it was painted. He gaped in amazement, fingers pressing into the wonder-white, soft bread of his sandwich.\
Inside, Eloise was the only occupant who hadn\'92t taken cover\'97no ducking, no diving under furniture, no flinging herself for a window. If they\'92d survived the first few seconds, they\'92d likely survive the actual strike (or at least, until the next order).\
She calmly grabbed her tablet, opened an app, and scanned telemetry from the offensive hardware outside. Onscreen, the simulation replayed: a PAPER gunship\'92s particle gun fired at the mansion; a tank returned fire at the gunship; a second gunship blew the tank apart. The whole engagement lasted less than eight-tenths of a second\'97the moment the trigger\'92s pulled, electronics and software do the rest. No pyrotechnic space opera; just short, precise violence. No paperwork, no refunds.\
The new instructions would be Eloise\'92s. She grinned. PAPER still believed their targets were in the other front room\'97and probably still did, convinced they\'92d been neutralised. Another textbook failure of intelligence, not hardware. After the obligatory authentication rituals, she accessed the firmware backdoors on every asset in play, compiled a list, and issued a theatre-wide shutdown. The gunships landed\'97ignoring their pilots\'97and powered off. The tanks froze, like frogs in a snow storm.\
It was unthinkable. In one move, Eloise had revealed she could disable all the weaponry on both sides.\

\f2\i Tax it
\f1\i0 , she thought. 
\f2\i I\'92m done selling boys\'92 toys to toy boys anyway
\f1\i0 . She\'92d never rule the world, not really, and snorted at the absurd grandiosity of such ambition\'97though deep in the innocent, tender recesses of her heart, she always hoped she might, one day.\
\'93C\'92mon. We\'92re leaving,\'94 Eloise told the three other women.\
Hayley instinctively took charge, opening the door to the hallway. A small avalanche of refuse rolled, slithered, and wafted into the parlour. Hayley jumped back, coughing as if her life depended on it.\
Eloise found the french doors to the patio locked. Kathy launched towards a window and squealed with fright as a creature-like shadow leapt onto the lace curtain. The shadow heaved the window up and stuck its threatening head in.\
\'93Mother!\'94 the creature cried. \'93Thank fortunes, you\'92re okay.\'94\
Eloise spun on Alexander. \'93What the tax happened? Did you poke those PAPER agents?\'94\
With the curtain draped about him like an oversized bridal veil\'97sheer, frilly, and ridiculous\'97Alexander looked like an over-sized sock puppet crashing the world\'92s most awkward wedding. \'93No, mother, and if I find out which idiot assistant producer put this scene on the call sheet\'97\'94\
\'93Get out of the way!\'94 Kathy barked. \'93Expectant mothers first.\'94\
\'93Twinkle Rump!\'94 Alexander reached through the window.\
\'93Wait!\'94 Eloise ordered. \'93We can\'92t expose Sarah to PAPER eyes yet.\'94 Eloise wasn\'92t about to risk any of them out there. Not yet. She pulled out her tablet again, calling up a device sniffer. The app displayed everything emitting within two kilometres of the nearest comms tower\'97even the clandestine ones.\
\'93Agent Jones is running the PAPER operation,\'94 Hayley reported. \'93He\'92s been chasing Sarah since\'97\'94\
Eloise hushed Hayley with a raised finger. 
\f2\i Wait
\f1\i0 . She spoke into her tablet, her tone so amicable you could mistake her for customer service. \'93Agent Jones, I presume? Very good. I just want to\'97no, no, Agent Jones, you\'92ll have to save that for another day\'85 unless you want all your expensive machinery in the immediate area to explode. No? Good. Now, listen carefully.\'94 She scrolled, voice drifting to a tone reserved for party invitations, diplomatic ultimatums, and mercy killings. \'93Presently, I\'92ll be leaving the premises in my limousine, with my son and three of my dearest friends. I expect\'97no, Agent Jones, I will do nothing of the kind, and I suggest you learn some manners, because if you want to rant at me, please keep it until after I\'92ve shared some very important information. Am I making myself clear? Good. I\'92ll take the sound of your grinding teeth as a yes.\
\'93Now, if you\'92re wondering how your gunships were disabled, you should consult the Warranties and Service, and Proprietary Rights provisions of your contract. If John Deere can stop a farmer from fixing his own tractor, I can certainly stop jarheads from blowing things up around me\'85 Yes, I understand your position, but you have violated the terms I have with your masters\'97people whose pay grades are so far above yours\'85 well, your salary is basically just pocket change at a lemonade stand. Yes, I don\'92t like lemonade either, but that\'92s beside the point.\
\'93My companions and I will be leaving safely, Agent Jones, because I have initiated a destruct sequence on all your hardware\'97all your gunships, all your particle pistols, and everything in between. So unless you fancy a bucket-sized hole where you banger and spuds once dangled, I suggest you provide every reasonable affordance for me to leave in peace. Then, and only then, I\'92ll cancel the detonation sequence. You have ten minutes from about\'85 oh! a minute and a half ago.\
\'93Do we have an understanding? Oh, you\'92re grinding your teeth again. Excellent. Good-bye, Agent Jones.\'94\
