\f1\fs22 Behind Sarah came Kathy, Eloise, and the detective. In a blink, Sarah was surrounded by people she\'92d rather be with, led away by Eloise toward the waiting limousine.\
The Elvi rallied, forming a loose barricade between them and Eloise\'92s ground car. One swung a guitar off her hip and struck a chord that sounded thin and disharmonious in the open air. The others filled their lungs, about to break into anthem.\
They never sang a note. Eloise strode up to the guitarist, plucked the instrument from her hands, and demolished it on the limousine\'92s hood. She hurled the twisted remains in a high arc\'97a grotesque cat o\'92 six tails flailing through the dusk.\
The Elvi turned as one, eyes wide. Eloise dusted her hands with the careful poise of someone flicking lint from cashmere, not a detail of makeup disturbed. She fixed the Elvi with a quiet, pointed sermon. Tony watched their bravado crumple; he didn\'92t hear the words, but he knew a veiled threat about the tanks when he saw one.\
Alexander scrambled into the front passenger seat; Eloise shepherded the others into the back.\
Tony\'92s heart cracked as the cavalcade rolled away\'97slow, cold, and stately, past silent tanks, out the gate, between watching gunships, away.\
\'93Hey!\'94 one of the Elvi called out, jogging over.\
Tony blinked. \'93Huh?\'94 It was the first sound he\'92d made since the attack, and it came out dry and scratchy. \
The Elvis pointed at what Tony had forgotten was in his hand. \'93You gonna eat that sandwich?\'94\
