\f0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 <!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 Inside the limousine, Eloise regarded the three women in the back seat. She read relief, gratitude, and a glint of steel behind their eyes. 
\f2\i I could buy each of you fifty times over
\f1\i0 , she thought, as she had bought so many\'97bright, loyal, brutal people. But not these women. They weren\'92t for sale\'97and perhaps, she allowed herself the rare pleasure of hope, with them in her employ, her odds had marginally improved.
